IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vic-nouns`
IMPORT `vic-interpretation-time`

-- Part III -- Provisions applicable to subordinate instruments, ss 22 to 34.
-- Ss 24 and 25 are time rules and live in vic-interpretation-time.l4.
-- The sections that mirror Part II are written out as the text prints them; where the two Parts differ in words, the difference is kept.

§ `Part III -- Provisions applicable to subordinate instruments`

§§ `s 22 Subordinate instruments to be construed subject to legislative power of the State and to empowering Act`

DECLARE VicLimitOnASubordinateInstrument IS ONE OF
    VicLegislativePowerOfTheStateOfVictoria
    VicPowerToMakeTheInstrumentConferredByTheEmpoweringAct

DECLARE VicEffectOfAInstrumentProvisionAgainstTheLimit IS ONE OF
    VicInstrumentOperatesFully
    VicInstrumentOperatesToTheExtentNotInExcessAndTheRemainderIsNotAffected

-- s 22(1): a subordinate instrument is construed as operating to the full extent of, but not exceeding, the legislative power of Victoria or the power to make it conferred by the Act; a provision in excess operates to the extent it is not in excess.
-- src:266 | (1) Every subordinate instrument shall be construed as operating to the full extent of, but so as not to exceed—
-- src:267 | (a) the legislative power of the State of Victoria; or
-- src:268 | (b) the power to make the subordinate instrument conferred by the Act under or pursuant to which it is made—
-- src:269 | to the intent that where a provision of a subordinate instrument, or the application of any such provision to any person, subject-matter or circumstance, would, but for this section, have been construed as being in excess of that power, it shall nevertheless be a valid provision to the extent to which it is not in excess of that power and the remainder of the subordinate instrument and the application of that provision to other persons, subject-matters or circumstances shall not be affected.
@ref s 22(1) (src:266-269)
GIVEN limit IS A VicLimitOnASubordinateInstrument, wouldOtherwiseBeInExcessOfThatPower IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A VicEffectOfAInstrumentProvisionAgainstTheLimit
`s22(1) how a provision of a subordinate instrument is construed against the limit of its power` MEANS
    IF wouldOtherwiseBeInExcessOfThatPower
    THEN VicInstrumentOperatesToTheExtentNotInExcessAndTheRemainderIsNotAffected
    ELSE VicInstrumentOperatesFully

-- s 22(2): the section is in addition to, and not in derogation of, any provision of the instrument or of the empowering Act relating to the construction or extent of operation of the instrument.
-- src:270 | (2) The provisions of this section are in addition to, and not in derogation of, any provision of a subordinate instrument or of the Act under or pursuant to which a subordinate instrument is made relating to the construction, or extent of the operation, of that subordinate instrument.
@ref s 22(2) (src:270)
GIVEN anotherProvisionOnConstructionOrExtentOfOperation IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s22(2) s 22 takes the place of a provision on the construction or extent of operation of the instrument` MEANS
    IF anotherProvisionOnConstructionOrExtentOfOperation THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 23 Construction of subordinate instruments`

-- s 23: where an Act confers power to make a subordinate instrument, expressions used in an instrument made in exercise of that power have, unless the contrary intention appears, the same meanings as in the Act as amended and in force for the time being.
-- src:272 | 23 Construction of subordinate instruments
-- src:273 | Where an Act confers power to make a subordinate instrument, expressions used in a subordinate instrument made in the exercise of that power shall, unless the contrary intention appears, have the same respective meanings as they have in the Act conferring the power as amended and in force for the time being.
@ref s 23 (src:272-273)
GIVEN madeInExerciseOfAPowerAnActConfers IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s23 an expression in the instrument has the same meaning as in the Act conferring the power` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT madeInExerciseOfAPowerAnActConfers THEN JUST FALSE
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 26 Exercise of powers between making and commencement of subordinate instruments`

-- s 26(1): applies where a subordinate instrument or provision that does not come into operation on its making will, on coming into operation, confer power (or amend another instrument to confer power) to make instruments, give notices, make appointments, establish a body, prescribe forms or do any other thing.
-- src:283 | (1) This section applies where a subordinate instrument or a provision of a subordinate instrument which does not come into operation immediately on the making of the subordinate instrument will, on its coming into operation, confer power or amend another subordinate instrument so as to confer power under the other subordinate instrument as so amended to—
-- src:284 | (a) make other subordinate instruments or any other instruments of a legislative or administrative character; or
-- src:285 | (b) give notices; or
-- src:286 | (c) make appointments; or
-- src:287 | (d) establish a body; or
-- src:288 | (e) prescribe forms; or
-- src:289 | (f) do any other thing—
-- src:290 | for the purposes of that subordinate instrument or provision or that other subordinate instrument.
@ref s 26(1) (src:283-290)
GIVEN doesNotComeIntoOperationOnMaking IS A BOOLEAN, willConferPowerOnComingIntoOperation IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s26(1) s 26 applies` MEANS
    IF doesNotComeIntoOperationOnMaking AND willConferPowerOnComingIntoOperation THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 26(2): unless the contrary intention appears, the power may be exercised at any time after the making of the instrument.
-- src:291 | (2) Unless the contrary intention appears, the power may be exercised at any time after the making of the subordinate instrument but its exercise does not confer a right or impose an obligation on a person before the coming into operation of the subordinate instrument or provision except insofar as is necessary or expedient for the purpose of—
-- src:292 | (a) bringing the subordinate instrument or provision into operation; or
-- src:293 | (b) making the subordinate instrument or provision or the other subordinate instrument as amended fully effective at or after that coming into operation.
@ref s 26(2) (src:291-293)
GIVEN section26Applies IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s26(2) the power may be exercised after the making and before the commencement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT section26Applies THEN JUST FALSE
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 26(2): its exercise does not confer a right or impose an obligation before the coming into operation, except insofar as necessary or expedient to bring the instrument or provision into operation or to make it fully effective.
-- src:291 | (2) Unless the contrary intention appears, the power may be exercised at any time after the making of the subordinate instrument but its exercise does not confer a right or impose an obligation on a person before the coming into operation of the subordinate instrument or provision except insofar as is necessary or expedient for the purpose of—
-- src:292 | (a) bringing the subordinate instrument or provision into operation; or
-- src:293 | (b) making the subordinate instrument or provision or the other subordinate instrument as amended fully effective at or after that coming into operation.
@ref s 26(2) (src:291-293)
GIVEN section26Applies IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN, necessaryOrExpedientToBringIntoOperation IS A BOOLEAN, necessaryOrExpedientToMakeFullyEffective IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s26(2) the exercise of the power confers a right or imposes an obligation before the commencement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT section26Applies THEN NOTHING
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN NOTHING
        IF necessaryOrExpedientToBringIntoOperation OR necessaryOrExpedientToMakeFullyEffective THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 26(3): without limiting subsection (2), an appointee may exercise a power, and a body may meet and exercise a power, before the coming into operation as if the instrument or provision were in operation.
-- src:294 | (3) Without limiting subsection (2), an appointee may exercise a power, and a body may meet and exercise a power, under that subsection before the coming into operation of the subordinate instrument or provision in the same manner and subject to the same conditions or limitations (if any) and with an entitlement to payment of the same remuneration or allowances (if any) as if the subordinate instrument or provision were in operation.
@ref s 26(3) (src:294)
GIVEN section26Applies IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s26(3) an appointee or body may exercise the power before the commencement as if the instrument were in operation` MEANS
    IF section26Applies THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 26(4): the term of office does not begin until the instrument or provision comes into operation.
-- src:295 | (4) For the purposes of any provision as to the duration of the term of office of an appointee (including a member of a body), that term does not begin until the coming into operation of the subordinate instrument or provision despite the exercise of any power under this section before that coming into operation.
@ref s 26(4) (src:295)
GIVEN dayOfQuestion IS A DATE, dayInstrumentOrProvisionComesIntoOperation IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s26(4) the term of office cannot yet begin` MEANS
    IF dayOfQuestion LESS THAN dayInstrumentOrProvisionComesIntoOperation THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 27 Implied power to repeal or amend subordinate instruments`

-- s 27: where an Act confers power to make a subordinate instrument, the power is, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, construed as including a power, exercisable in the same manner and subject to the same conditions or limitations, to repeal or amend an instrument made in exercise of that power.
-- src:297 | 27 Implied power to repeal or amend subordinate instruments
-- src:298 | Where an Act confers power to make a subordinate instrument the power shall, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, be construed as including a power, exercisable in the same manner and subject to the same conditions or limitations (if any), to repeal or amend a subordinate instrument made in the exercise of that power.
@ref s 27 (src:297-298)
GIVEN anActConfersPowerToMakeTheInstrument IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s27 the power to make the instrument includes a power to repeal or amend it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT anActConfersPowerToMakeTheInstrument THEN JUST FALSE
        IF contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 28 Provisions as to effect of repeal etc. of subordinate instruments`

-- s 28(1): a subordinate instrument or provision that had been repealed by the first-mentioned one is not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, construed as revived.
-- src:301 | (1) Where a subordinate instrument or a provision of a subordinate instrument—
-- src:302 | (a) is repealed; or
-- src:303 | (b) expires, lapses or otherwise ceases to have effect—
-- src:304 | any subordinate instrument or provision of a subordinate instrument that had been repealed by the first-mentioned subordinate instrument or provision shall not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, be construed as having been revived in consequence of the repeal, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect of the first-mentioned subordinate instrument or provision.
@ref s 28(1) (src:301-304)
GIVEN event IS A VicEndOfOperation, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s28(1) the instrument or provision that the ending instrument or provision had repealed is construed as revived` MEANS
    IF contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE VicThingTheEndingOfAnInstrumentMightAffect IS ONE OF
    VicInstrumentAnythingNotInForceOrExistingAtThatTime              -- (c)
    VicInstrumentThePreviousOperationOrAnythingDulyDoneOrSuffered    -- (d)
    VicInstrumentARightPrivilegeObligationOrLiabilityAcquiredAccruedOrIncurred   -- (e)
    VicInstrumentAPenaltyForfeitureOrPunishmentIncurredForAnOffence  -- (f)
    VicInstrumentAnythingElse

-- s 28(2)(c) to (f): the repeal, amendment, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect does not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, revive or affect the thing. (There is no paragraph for an immunity or indemnity in this section.)
-- src:305 | (2) Where a subordinate instrument or a provision of a subordinate instrument—
-- src:306 | (a) is repealed or amended; or
-- src:307 | (b) expires, lapses or otherwise ceases to have effect—
-- src:308 | the repeal, amendment, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect of that subordinate instrument or provision shall not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears—
-- src:309 | (c) revive anything not in force or existing at the time at which the repeal, amendment, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect becomes operative;
-- src:310 | (d) affect the previous operation of that subordinate instrument or provision or anything duly done or suffered under that subordinate instrument or provision;
-- src:311 | (e) affect any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under that subordinate instrument or provision;
-- src:312 | (f) affect any penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of any offence committed against that subordinate instrument or provision; or
-- src:313 | (g) affect any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of any such right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment as is mentioned in paragraphs (e) and (f)—
-- src:314 | and any such investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, and any such penalty, forfeiture or punishment may be imposed, as if that subordinate instrument or provision had not been repealed or amended or had not expired, lapsed or otherwise ceased to have effect.
@ref s 28(2) (src:305-314)
GIVEN thing IS A VicThingTheEndingOfAnInstrumentMightAffect, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s28(2)(c)-(f) the repeal, amendment, expiry or lapsing revives or affects the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN VicInstrumentAnythingElse THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE IF contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 28(2)(g): it does not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, affect an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of a right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment mentioned in paragraphs (e) and (f).
-- src:313 | (g) affect any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of any such right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment as is mentioned in paragraphs (e) and (f)—
@ref s 28(2)(g) (src:313)
GIVEN inRespectOfARightLiabilityOrPenalty IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s28(2)(g) the repeal, amendment, expiry or lapsing affects an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT inRespectOfARightLiabilityOrPenalty THEN NOTHING
        IF contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 28(2), closing words: any such investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, and any such penalty, forfeiture or punishment may be imposed, as if the instrument or provision had not been repealed, amended, expired, lapsed or ceased to have effect.
-- src:305 | (2) Where a subordinate instrument or a provision of a subordinate instrument—
-- src:306 | (a) is repealed or amended; or
-- src:307 | (b) expires, lapses or otherwise ceases to have effect—
-- src:308 | the repeal, amendment, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect of that subordinate instrument or provision shall not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears—
-- src:309 | (c) revive anything not in force or existing at the time at which the repeal, amendment, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect becomes operative;
-- src:310 | (d) affect the previous operation of that subordinate instrument or provision or anything duly done or suffered under that subordinate instrument or provision;
-- src:311 | (e) affect any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under that subordinate instrument or provision;
-- src:312 | (f) affect any penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of any offence committed against that subordinate instrument or provision; or
-- src:313 | (g) affect any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of any such right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment as is mentioned in paragraphs (e) and (f)—
-- src:314 | and any such investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, and any such penalty, forfeiture or punishment may be imposed, as if that subordinate instrument or provision had not been repealed or amended or had not expired, lapsed or otherwise ceased to have effect.
@ref s 28(2) (src:305-314)
GIVEN inRespectOfARightLiabilityOrPenalty IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s28(2) the proceeding may be instituted, continued or enforced, or the penalty imposed, as if the instrument had not been repealed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT inRespectOfARightLiabilityOrPenalty THEN NOTHING
        IF contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 28(2A): the same protection for a savings or transitional provision, a provision that makes a thing effective that would otherwise be ineffective, or one requiring a reference to an entity to be construed as a reference to another.
-- src:316 | (2A) Without limiting subsection (2), if a provision of a subordinate instrument that is of a savings or transitional nature (whether or not the subordinate instrument describes it as such) or that validates anything that is or may otherwise be invalid or that requires a reference in a subordinate instrument or Act or other instrument or document to, or that relates to, an entity or a class of entity to be construed as a reference to another entity or class of entity—
-- src:317 | (a) is repealed; or
-- src:318 | (b) expires, lapses or otherwise ceases to have effect—
-- src:319 | the repeal, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect of that provision does not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, affect the operation of the savings or transitional provision or end the validating effect of the provision or affect the construction of that reference, as the case requires.
@ref s 28(2A) (src:316-319)
GIVEN kindOfProvision IS A VicProvisionProtectedOnRepeal, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s28(2A) the repeal, expiry or lapsing of the provision ends the effect it had` MEANS
    CONSIDER kindOfProvision
    WHEN VicAnyOtherProvision THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE IF contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 28(3): references in subsections (1), (2) and (2A) to repeal include a repeal by implication and a repeal by abrogating or limiting the effect of the instrument or provision or excluding its application.
-- src:321 | (3) References in subsections (1), (2) and (2A) to the repeal of a subordinate instrument or of a provision of a subordinate instrument shall be construed as including references to—
-- src:322 | (a) a repeal effected by implication; and
-- src:323 | (b) a repeal effected by abrogating or limiting the effect of the subordinate instrument or provision or excluding the application of the subordinate instrument or provision to any person, subject-matter or circumstance.
@ref s 28(3) (src:321-323)
GIVEN how IS A VicHowRepealed
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s28(3) the way of repealing is within the references to repeal in s 28(1), (2) and (2A)` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN VicRepealedExpressly THEN NOTHING
    WHEN VicRepealedByImplication THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN VicRepealedByAbrogatingOrLimitingItsEffect THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN VicRepealedByExcludingItsApplication THEN JUST TRUE

§§ `s 29 Effect of repeal etc. of amending subordinate instrument`

-- s 29(1): the ending of an instrument or provision that directly amended another instrument or an Act does not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, affect the direct amendments or their operation or effect.
-- src:326 | (1) Where a subordinate instrument or a provision of a subordinate instrument, being a subordinate instrument or provision that directly amended another subordinate instrument or an Act (whether by the insertion of words or expressions in that subordinate instrument or Act or the substitution of other words or expressions for words or expressions in that subordinate instrument or Act)—
-- src:327 | (a) is repealed; or
-- src:328 | (b) expires, lapses or otherwise ceases to have effect—
-- src:329 | the repeal, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect of that subordinate instrument or provision shall not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, affect in any way the direct amendments made in the other subordinate instrument or in the Act or the operation or effect of those amendments.
@ref s 29(1) (src:326-329)
GIVEN directlyAmendedByInsertionOrSubstitutionOfWords IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s29(1) the ending of the amending instrument or provision affects the direct amendments` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT directlyAmendedByInsertionOrSubstitutionOfWords THEN NOTHING
        IF contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 29(2): subsection (1) applies to a direct amendment made to a provision of an instrument by another provision of that instrument.
-- src:330 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to a direct amendment made to a provision of a subordinate instrument by another provision of that subordinate instrument in the same manner as it applies to a direct amendment made to a subordinate instrument by another subordinate instrument.
@ref s 29(2) (src:330)
GIVEN amendedByAnotherProvisionOfTheSameInstrument IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s29(2) s 29(1) applies to the amendment` MEANS
    IF amendedByAnotherProvisionOfTheSameInstrument THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 30 Repeal and re-making`

-- s 30(a): where a subordinate instrument or provision is repealed and re-made, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, a reference in any instrument or Act to the repealed one is construed as a reference to the re-made one.
-- src:334 | (a) any reference in any subordinate instrument or Act to the repealed subordinate instrument or provision shall be construed as a reference to the re-made subordinate instrument or provision; and
@ref s 30(a) (src:334)
GIVEN repealedAndReMade IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s30(a) a reference to the repealed instrument or provision is construed as a reference to the re-made instrument or provision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT repealedAndReMade THEN JUST FALSE
        IF contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 30(b): insofar as an instrument made or thing done under the repealed one could have been made or done under the re-made one, it has effect as if made or done under the re-made one.
-- src:335 | (b) insofar as any subordinate instrument made or other thing done under the repealed subordinate instrument or provision, or having effect as if so made or done, could have been made or done under the re-made subordinate instrument or provision, it shall have effect as if made or done under the re-made subordinate instrument or provision.
@ref s 30(b) (src:335)
GIVEN repealedAndReMade IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN, couldHaveBeenMadeOrDoneUnderTheReMadeProvision IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s30(b) the instrument made or thing done has effect as if made or done under the re-made instrument or provision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT repealedAndReMade THEN JUST FALSE
        IF contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        IF couldHaveBeenMadeOrDoneUnderTheReMadeProvision THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 31 Construction of references in subordinate instruments to other enactments`

-- s 31(1): a reference in a subordinate instrument to itself or any provision of it, any other instrument or provision, or any Act or provision of an Act is, unless the contrary intention appears, construed according to what has become of it.
-- src:339 | (1) A reference in a subordinate instrument to that subordinate instrument or to any provision of that subordinate instrument or to any other subordinate instrument or to any provision of any other subordinate instrument or to any Act or provision of an Act shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed—
-- src:340 | (a) if the subordinate instrument, Act or provision in question has been amended, as a reference to the subordinate instrument, Act or provision as amended and in force for the time being;
-- src:341 | (b) if the subordinate instrument, Act or provision in question has been re-made or re-enacted (with or without modification), as a reference to the subordinate instrument, Act or provision as re-made or re-enacted and in force for the time being;
-- src:342 | (c) if the subordinate instrument, Act or provision in question has been re-made or re-enacted (with or without modification) and subsequently amended, as a reference to the subordinate instrument, Act or provision as re-made or re-enacted and as subsequently amended and in force for the time being; and
-- src:343 | (d) if the subordinate instrument, Act or provision in question has been repealed and not re-enacted or re-made, as a reference to the Act, subordinate instrument or provision as in force immediately before its repeal.
@ref s 31(1) (src:339-343)
GIVEN state IS A VicStateOfEnactmentReferredTo, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE VicReadsAs
`s31(1) a reference in a subordinate instrument to another enactment is construed as a reference to` MEANS
    IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER state
         WHEN VicStillAsFirstMade THEN NOTHING
         WHEN VicHasBeenAmended THEN JUST VicTheEnactmentAsAmendedAndInForceForTheTimeBeing
         WHEN VicHasBeenReEnactedOrReMade THEN JUST VicTheEnactmentAsReEnactedOrReMadeAndInForceForTheTimeBeing
         WHEN VicHasBeenReEnactedOrReMadeAndSubsequentlyAmended THEN JUST VicTheEnactmentAsReEnactedOrReMadeAndSubsequentlyAmendedAndInForceForTheTimeBeing
         WHEN VicHasBeenRepealedAndNotReEnactedOrReMade THEN JUST VicTheEnactmentAsInForceImmediatelyBeforeItsRepeal

-- s 31(1A): a reference in a subordinate instrument to a provision of an instrument or Act that has been renumbered or relocated is construed as a reference to it as renumbered or relocated and in force for the time being, unless the contrary intention appears.
-- src:345 | (1A) A reference in a subordinate instrument to any provision of that or any other subordinate instrument or to any provision of an Act must, if the provision in question has been renumbered or relocated, be construed as a reference to the provision as renumbered or relocated and in force for the time being, unless the contrary intention appears.
@ref s 31(1A) (src:345)
GIVEN referenceIsToAProvision IS A BOOLEAN, provisionRenumberedOrRelocated IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE VicReadsAs
`s31(1A) a reference in a subordinate instrument to a provision that has been renumbered or relocated is construed as a reference to` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT referenceIsToAProvision THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT provisionRenumberedOrRelocated THEN NOTHING
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST VicTheProvisionAsRenumberedOrRelocatedAndInForceForTheTimeBeing

DECLARE VicLegislationOfAnotherPlaceForSection31 IS ONE OF
    VicACommonwealthActS31
    VicAnActOrOrdinanceOfAnotherStateOrOfATerritoryS31
    VicAnInstrumentOfALegislativeCharacterMadeUnderACommonwealthActS31
    VicAnInstrumentOfALegislativeCharacterMadeUnderAnActOrOrdinanceOfAnotherStateOrOfATerritoryS31
    VicAnythingElseS31

-- s 31(2)(a): in s 31, a reference to an Act includes a Commonwealth Act and an Act or Ordinance of another State or of a Territory.
-- src:348 | (a) a reference to an Act includes a reference to—
-- src:349 | (i) a Commonwealth Act; and
-- src:350 | (ii) an Act or Ordinance of another State or of a Territory;
@ref s 31(2)(a) (src:348-350)
GIVEN thing IS A VicLegislationOfAnotherPlaceForSection31
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s31(2)(a) a reference to an Act in s 31 includes` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN VicACommonwealthActS31 THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN VicAnActOrOrdinanceOfAnotherStateOrOfATerritoryS31 THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 31(2)(b): in s 31, a reference to a subordinate instrument includes an instrument of a legislative character made or to be made under a Commonwealth Act or under an Act or Ordinance of another State or of a Territory (the text joins the two limbs with "or" here and with "and" in s 17(2)(b)).
-- src:351 | (b) a reference to a subordinate instrument includes a reference to an instrument of a legislative character made or to be made under or pursuant to the provisions of—
-- src:352 | (i) a Commonwealth Act; or
-- src:353 | (ii) an Act or Ordinance of another State or of a Territory.
@ref s 31(2)(b) (src:351-353)
GIVEN thing IS A VicLegislationOfAnotherPlaceForSection31
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s31(2)(b) a reference to a subordinate instrument in s 31 includes` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN VicAnInstrumentOfALegislativeCharacterMadeUnderACommonwealthActS31 THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN VicAnInstrumentOfALegislativeCharacterMadeUnderAnActOrOrdinanceOfAnotherStateOrOfATerritoryS31 THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 32 Prescribing matters by reference to other documents`

-- s 32(1): relevant day means the day on which the Interpretation of Legislation (Amendment) Act 1991 comes into operation. That Act is not among the sources, so its commencement day is supplied.
-- src:375 | relevant day means the day on which the Interpretation of Legislation (Amendment) Act 1991 comes into operation.
@ref s 32(1) "relevant day" (src:375)
GIVEN dayTheAmendmentActOf1991CameIntoOperation IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s32(1) relevant day` MEANS dayTheAmendmentActOf1991CameIntoOperation

-- s 32(1): Code means one of the named Codes and Laws, any other Code to which the 1981 Application of Laws Act applies (para (f)), or a regulation or rule having the force of law in Victoria made under one of paragraphs (a) to (l) (para (m)).
-- src:359 | Code means—
-- src:360 | (a) the Companies (Victoria) Code;
-- src:361 | (b) the Companies (Acquisition of Shares) (Victoria) Code;
-- src:362 | (c) the Futures Industry (Victoria) Code;
-- src:363 | (d) the Securities Industry (Victoria) Code;
-- src:364 | (e) the Companies and Securities (Interpretation and Miscellaneous Provisions) (Victoria) Code;
-- src:365 | (f) any other Code to which the Companies and Securities (Interpretation and Miscellaneous Provisions) (Application of Laws) Act 1981 applies;
-- src:366 | (g) the ASIC Law of Victoria;
-- src:367 | (h) the Corporations Law of Victoria;
-- src:368 | (ha) the National Electricity (Victoria) Law;
-- src:369 | (i) the AFIC (Victoria) Code;
-- src:370 | (j) the Financial Institutions (Victoria) Code;
-- src:371 | (ja) the National Gas (Victoria) Law;
-- src:373 | (l) the Friendly Societies (Victoria) Code;
-- src:374 | (m) a regulation or rule that has the force of law in Victoria made under a Code or Law referred to in paragraphs (a) to (l);
@ref s 32(1) "Code" (src:359-374)
GIVEN name IS A STRING, otherCodeToWhichThe1981ApplicationOfLawsActApplies IS A BOOLEAN, regulationOrRuleWithForceOfLawMadeUnderAnAToLCode IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s32(1) the thing is a Code` MEANS
    elem name (LIST "the Companies (Victoria) Code", "the Companies (Acquisition of Shares) (Victoria) Code", "the Futures Industry (Victoria) Code", "the Securities Industry (Victoria) Code", "the Companies and Securities (Interpretation and Miscellaneous Provisions) (Victoria) Code", "the ASIC Law of Victoria", "the Corporations Law of Victoria", "the National Electricity (Victoria) Law", "the AFIC (Victoria) Code", "the Financial Institutions (Victoria) Code", "the National Gas (Victoria) Law", "the Friendly Societies (Victoria) Code")
        OR otherCodeToWhichThe1981ApplicationOfLawsActApplies
        OR regulationOrRuleWithForceOfLawMadeUnderAnAToLCode

DECLARE VicMatterAppliedByASubordinateInstrument IS ONE OF
    VicAnActApplied
    VicACommonwealthActApplied
    VicACodeApplied
    VicAStatutoryRuleApplied
    VicAStatutoryRuleMadeUnderACommonwealthActApplied
    VicAnyOtherDocumentApplied

DECLARE VicTimeOfApplication IS ONE OF
    VicAsInForceAtAParticularTime
    VicAsInForceFromTimeToTime

-- s 32(2): if an Act authorises or requires provision to be made by a subordinate instrument, the instrument, if made on or after the relevant day and unless the contrary intention appears in the Act, (a) may apply, adopt or incorporate an Act, a Commonwealth Act, a Code, a statutory rule or a Commonwealth statutory rule, as in force at a particular time or from time to time; and (b) must not do so for a matter in any other document.
-- src:378 | (2) If an Act (whether passed before or after the relevant day) authorises or requires provision to be made for or in relation to a matter by a subordinate instrument, the subordinate instrument, if made on or after the relevant day and unless the contrary intention appears in the Act under or pursuant to which it is made—
-- src:379 | (a) may make provision for or in relation to that matter by applying, adopting or incorporating, with or without modification, the provisions of—
-- src:380 | (i) an Act; or
-- src:382 | (ia) a Commonwealth Act; or
-- src:383 | (ii) a Code; or
-- src:385 | (iii) a statutory rule; or
-- src:387 | (iv) a statutory rule (within the meaning of the Statutory Rules Publication Act 1903 of the Commonwealth) made under a Commonwealth Act—
-- src:388 | as in force at a particular time or as in force from time to time; and
-- src:390 | (b) must not make provision for or in relation to that matter by applying, adopting or incorporating any matter contained in a document (not being an Act, Commonwealth Act, Code, statutory rule or statutory rule made under a Commonwealth Act).
@ref s 32(2) (src:378-390)
GIVEN authorisedOrRequiredByAnAct IS A BOOLEAN, madeOn IS A DATE, relevantDay IS A DATE, contraryIntentionAppearsInTheAct IS A BOOLEAN, matter IS A VicMatterAppliedByASubordinateInstrument, timeOfApplication IS A VicTimeOfApplication
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s32(2) the subordinate instrument may apply, adopt or incorporate the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT authorisedOrRequiredByAnAct THEN JUST FALSE
        IF madeOn LESS THAN relevantDay THEN JUST FALSE
        IF contraryIntentionAppearsInTheAct THEN JUST FALSE
        IF matter EQUALS VicAnyOtherDocumentApplied THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE VicPlaceOfInspection IS ONE OF
    VicTheDepartmentOfTheMinisterOrAnotherPublicOfficeTheMinisterSpecifiesByGazetteNotice
    VicThePrincipalOfficeOfTheBodyThatMadeTheInstrumentOrAnotherPublicOfficeTheMinisterSpecifiesByGazetteNotice

-- s 32(3)(a): where an instrument made on or after the relevant day applies a document that is not an Act, Commonwealth Act, Code or statutory rule, the Minister must, if the instrument is itself required to be laid before each House, cause a copy to be lodged with the Clerk of the Parliaments, notice to be published in the Government Gazette, and a copy of the notice to be laid before each House, each as soon as practicable after the step before.
-- src:394 | (a) the Minister administering the Act under which the subordinate instrument was made must if the subordinate instrument is itself required to be laid before each House of the Parliament cause—
-- src:395 | (i) a copy of the matter so applied, adopted or incorporated to be lodged with the Clerk of the Parliaments as soon as practicable after the subordinate instrument is required to be laid before each House of the Parliament; and
-- src:396 | (ii) notice of the documents containing the matter so applied, adopted or incorporated and of the fact that a copy of the matter so applied, adopted or incorporated has been lodged with the Clerk of the Parliaments, to be published in the Government Gazette as soon as practicable after the copy of the matter has been lodged; and
-- src:397 | (iii) a copy of the notice published in the Government Gazette to be laid before each House of the Parliament as soon as practicable after it is published; and
@ref s 32(3)(a) (src:394-397)
GIVEN instrumentMadeOnOrAfterRelevantDay IS A BOOLEAN, appliesAnyOtherDocument IS A BOOLEAN, instrumentRequiredToBeLaidBeforeEachHouse IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s32(3)(a) the Minister must cause the copy to be lodged, the notice published and the notice laid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (instrumentMadeOnOrAfterRelevantDay AND appliesAnyOtherDocument) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF instrumentRequiredToBeLaidBeforeEachHouse THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 32(3)(b): a copy of the matter must be kept available for inspection during normal office hours by members of the public without charge, at the place the paragraph names.
-- src:399 | (b) a copy of the matter so applied, adopted or incorporated must be kept available for inspection during normal office hours by members of the public without charge—
-- src:400 | (i) in the case of a subordinate instrument that is a statutory rule, at the Department of the Minister administering the Act under which the subordinate instrument is made or at some other appropriate public office specified by the Minister by a notice published in the Government Gazette; and
-- src:401 | (ii) in the case of a subordinate instrument that is not a statutory rule, at the principal office of the body which made the subordinate instrument or at some other appropriate public office specified by the Minister administering the Act under which it is made by a notice published in the Government Gazette.
@ref s 32(3)(b) (src:399-401)
GIVEN instrumentIsAStatutoryRule IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A VicPlaceOfInspection
`s32(3)(b) where a copy of the matter is kept available for inspection by the public without charge` MEANS
    IF instrumentIsAStatutoryRule
    THEN VicTheDepartmentOfTheMinisterOrAnotherPublicOfficeTheMinisterSpecifiesByGazetteNotice
    ELSE VicThePrincipalOfficeOfTheBodyThatMadeTheInstrumentOrAnotherPublicOfficeTheMinisterSpecifiesByGazetteNotice

-- s 32(4)(a): the same duties of the Minister arise when the matter applied, adopted or incorporated is later amended.
-- src:405 | (a) the Minister administering the Act under which the subordinate instrument was made must, if the subordinate instrument is itself required to be laid before each House of the Parliament, cause—
-- src:406 | (i) a copy of the matter as so amended to be lodged with the Clerk of the Parliaments as soon as practicable after that amendment is made; and
-- src:407 | (ii) notice of the amendment and the documents containing that amendment and of the fact that a copy of the matter as so amended has been lodged with the Clerk of the Parliaments, to be published in the Government Gazette as soon as practicable after the copy of the matter has been lodged; and
-- src:408 | (iii) a copy of the notice published in the Government Gazette to be laid before each House of the Parliament as soon as practicable after it is published; and
@ref s 32(4)(a) (src:405-408)
GIVEN instrumentMadeOnOrAfterRelevantDay IS A BOOLEAN, appliesAnyOtherDocumentAsInForceFromTimeToTime IS A BOOLEAN, matterIsAmendedAfterTheInstrumentIsMade IS A BOOLEAN, instrumentRequiredToBeLaidBeforeEachHouse IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s32(4)(a) the Minister must cause the amended copy to be lodged, the notice published and the notice laid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (instrumentMadeOnOrAfterRelevantDay AND appliesAnyOtherDocumentAsInForceFromTimeToTime AND matterIsAmendedAfterTheInstrumentIsMade) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF instrumentRequiredToBeLaidBeforeEachHouse THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 32(4)(c): a copy of the matter as amended must be kept available for inspection in the same way.
-- src:411 | (c) a copy of the matter as amended must be kept available for inspection during normal office hours by members of the public without charge—
-- src:412 | (i) in the case of a subordinate instrument that is a statutory rule, at the Department of the Minister administering the Act under which the subordinate instrument is made or at some other appropriate public office specified by the Minister by a notice published in the Government Gazette; and
-- src:413 | (ii) in the case of a subordinate instrument that is not a statutory rule, at the principal office of the body which made the subordinate instrument or at some other appropriate public office specified by the Minister administering the Act under which it is made by a notice published in the Government Gazette.
@ref s 32(4)(c) (src:411-413)
GIVEN instrumentIsAStatutoryRule IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A VicPlaceOfInspection
`s32(4)(c) where a copy of the amended matter is kept available for inspection by the public without charge` MEANS
    IF instrumentIsAStatutoryRule
    THEN VicTheDepartmentOfTheMinisterOrAnotherPublicOfficeTheMinisterSpecifiesByGazetteNotice
    ELSE VicThePrincipalOfficeOfTheBodyThatMadeTheInstrumentOrAnotherPublicOfficeTheMinisterSpecifiesByGazetteNotice

-- s 32(5): a failure to comply with subsection (3) or (4) does not affect the operation or effect of the subordinate instrument or its standing.
-- src:414 | (5) A failure to comply with subsection (3) or (4) does not affect the validity, operation or effect of the subordinate instrument.
@ref s 32(5) (src:414)
GIVEN failedToComplyWithSubsection3Or4 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s32(5) a failure to comply with s 32(3) or (4) affects the operation or effect of the instrument` MEANS
    IF failedToComplyWithSubsection3Or4 THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 32(12)(a): despite subsection (5), a person must not be convicted of an offence consisting of a contravention of an instrument made on or after the relevant day if it is proved that, at the time of the alleged contravention, a copy of the matter applied could not be inspected as the section provides.
-- src:421 | (a) must not be convicted of an offence consisting of a contravention of a subordinate instrument made on or after the relevant day if it is proved that, at the time of the alleged contravention; and
@ref s 32(12)(a) (src:421)
GIVEN instrumentMadeOnOrAfterRelevantDay IS A BOOLEAN, provedThatACopyCouldNotBeInspectedAtTheTimeOfTheAllegedContravention IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s32(12)(a) the person may be convicted of the offence of contravening the instrument` MEANS
    IF instrumentMadeOnOrAfterRelevantDay AND provedThatACopyCouldNotBeInspectedAtTheTimeOfTheAllegedContravention THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 32(12)(b): despite subsection (5), a person is not prejudicially affected or made subject to any liability by an instrument made on or after the relevant day if it is proved that, at the relevant time, a copy could not be inspected as the section provides.
-- src:422 | (b) is not prejudicially affected or made subject to any liability by a subordinate instrument made on or after the relevant day if it is proved that, at the relevant time—
@ref s 32(12)(b) (src:422)
GIVEN instrumentMadeOnOrAfterRelevantDay IS A BOOLEAN, provedThatACopyCouldNotBeInspectedAtTheRelevantTime IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s32(12)(b) the person is prejudicially affected or subject to a liability by the instrument` MEANS
    IF instrumentMadeOnOrAfterRelevantDay AND provedThatACopyCouldNotBeInspectedAtTheRelevantTime THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 32(13): despite any rule of law to the contrary, salaries, wages, fees, allowances or expenses payable to a person or class that may be prescribed by a subordinate instrument may be prescribed by reference to those payable to another person or class under any other Act or Commonwealth Act from time to time.
-- src:425 | (13) Despite any rule of law to the contrary, where salaries, wages, fees, allowances or expenses payable to any person or class of persons may be prescribed, determined or fixed by a subordinate instrument, whether or not the power to prescribe is subject to conditions, restrictions or limitations, the salaries, wages, fees, allowances or expenses may be prescribed, determined or fixed by the subordinate instrument by reference in that subordinate instrument to the salaries, wages, fees, allowances or expenses prescribed, determined or fixed by or under any other Act or by or under any Commonwealth Act from time to time as payable to any other person or class of persons.
@ref s 32(13) (src:425)
GIVEN maybePrescribedBySubordinateInstrument IS A BOOLEAN, byReferenceToThosePayableUnderAnotherActOrACommonwealthActFromTimeToTime IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s32(13) the amounts may be prescribed by reference to those fixed under another Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT maybePrescribedBySubordinateInstrument THEN JUST FALSE
        IF byReferenceToThosePayableUnderAnotherActOrACommonwealthActFromTimeToTime THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 32(13A) and (13B): the same for conditions of office, whether or not the power is subject to conditions, restrictions or limitations, and despite any rule of law to the contrary.
-- src:427 | (13A) If a subordinate instrument may prescribe, determine or fix any conditions of office for any person or class of persons, those conditions of office may be prescribed, determined or fixed by the subordinate instrument by reference in that subordinate instrument to the conditions of office applicable to any other person or class of persons prescribed, determined or fixed from time to time—
-- src:428 | (a) by or under any other Act; or
-- src:429 | (b) by or under any Commonwealth Act.
@ref s 32(13A) (src:427-429)
GIVEN maybePrescribedBySubordinateInstrument IS A BOOLEAN, byReferenceToConditionsOfOfficeUnderAnotherActOrACommonwealthActFromTimeToTime IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s32(13A) the conditions of office may be prescribed by reference to those fixed under another Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT maybePrescribedBySubordinateInstrument THEN JUST FALSE
        IF byReferenceToConditionsOfOfficeUnderAnotherActOrACommonwealthActFromTimeToTime THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:431 | (13B) Subsection (13A) applies—
-- src:432 | (a) whether or not the power to prescribe, determine or fix by subordinate instrument is subject to conditions, restrictions or limitations; and
-- src:433 | (b) despite any rule of law to the contrary.
@ref s 32(13B) (src:431-433)
GIVEN powerIsSubjectToConditionsRestrictionsOrLimitations IS A BOOLEAN, ruleOfLawToTheContraryExists IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s32(13B) s 32(13A) applies` MEANS
    JUST TRUE

-- s 32(14): a document or matter is not applied, adopted or incorporated by reason only that it is referred to, if it does not affect the operation of the subordinate instrument.
-- src:434 | (14) A document or matter is not applied, adopted or incorporated in a subordinate instrument by reason only that it is referred to in the subordinate instrument, or in another document or other matter applied, adopted or incorporated in the subordinate instrument, if the document or matter so referred to does not affect the operation of the subordinate instrument.
@ref s 32(14) (src:434)
GIVEN isOnlyReferredTo IS A BOOLEAN, doesNotAffectTheOperationOfTheInstrument IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s32(14) the document or matter is applied, adopted or incorporated` MEANS
    IF isOnlyReferredTo AND doesNotAffectTheOperationOfTheInstrument THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 33 Citation of references in regulations, rules, by-laws and local laws`

DECLARE VicUnitCitedByNumberInASubordinateInstrument IS ONE OF
    VicSiChapter
    VicSiPart
    VicSiRegulationRuleByLawLocalLawOrSchedule
    VicSiScheduleNotCitedByNumber
    VicSiDivision
    VicSiSubdivision
    VicSiSubregulationOrClauseOfARegulation
    VicSiSubruleOrClauseOfARule
    VicSiClauseOfAByLawOrLocalLaw
    VicSiParagraphOfAProvisionInterpretationOrSchedule
    VicSiParagraphOfAClauseSubclauseItemColumnTableOrFormInASchedule
    VicSiSubparagraph
    VicSiSubSubparagraph
    VicSiClauseItemColumnTableOrFormOfASchedule
    VicSiSubclause
    VicSiSubSubclause

-- s 33(1): where a provision of a subordinate instrument containing a regulation, rule, by-law or local law refers to a unit by a number, the reference is, unless the context otherwise requires, construed as a reference to the unit so designated in the place the paragraph names.
-- src:440 | (1) Where a provision of a subordinate instrument containing a regulation, rule, by-law or local law refers—
-- src:442 | (aaa) to a Chapter by a number, the reference shall, unless the context otherwise requires, be construed as a reference to the Chapter, designated by that number, of the subordinate instrument in which the reference occurs;
-- src:444 | (aa) to a Part by a number, the reference shall, unless the context otherwise requires, be construed—
-- src:445 | (i) if the subordinate instrument contains Chapters, as a reference to the Part, designated by that number, of the Chapter in which the reference occurs; or
-- src:446 | (ii) if the subordinate instrument does not contain Chapters, as a reference to the Part, designated by that number, of the subordinate instrument in which the reference occurs;
-- src:448 | (a) to a regulation, rule, by-law, local law or Schedule by a number, the reference shall, unless the context otherwise requires, be construed as a reference to the regulation, rule, by-law, local law or Schedule, designated by that number, of or to the subordinate instrument in which the reference occurs;
-- src:449 | (b) to a Schedule but does not refer to it by a number, the reference shall, unless the context otherwise requires, if there is only one Schedule to the subordinate instrument in which the reference occurs, be construed as a reference to the Schedule to the subordinate instrument in which the reference occurs; or
-- src:450 | (c) to a Division, Subdivision, subregulation, subrule, clause of a by-law, paragraph, subparagraph, sub-subparagraph, clause, subclause, sub-subclause, item, column, table or form by a number, the reference shall, unless the context otherwise requires, be construed as a reference—
-- src:451 | (i) to the Division, designated by that number, of the Part in which the reference occurs;
-- src:452 | (ii) to the Subdivision, designated by that number, of the Division in which the reference occurs;
-- src:453 | (iii) to the subregulation or clause, designated by that number, of the regulation in which the reference occurs;
-- src:454 | (iv) to the subrule or clause, designated by that number, of the rule in which the reference occurs;
-- src:456 | (v) to the clause, designated by that number, of the by-law or local law in which the reference occurs;
-- src:458 | (vi) to the paragraph, designated by that number, of the regulation, rule, by-law, local law, subregulation, subrule, clause of a by-law, local law, clause, subclause, interpretation or Schedule in which the reference occurs;
-- src:459 | (vii) to the paragraph, designated by that number, of the clause, subclause, item, column, table or form or in the Schedule in which the reference occurs;
-- src:460 | (viii) to the subparagraph, designated by that number, of the paragraph in which the reference occurs;
-- src:461 | (ix) to the sub-subparagraph, designated by that number, of the subparagraph in which the reference occurs;
-- src:462 | (x) to the clause, item, column, table or form, designated by that number, of or in the Schedule in which the reference occurs;
-- src:463 | (xi) to the subclause, designated by that number, of the clause in which the reference occurs; or
-- src:464 | (xii) to the sub-subclause, designated by that number, of the subclause in which the reference occurs—
-- src:465 | as the case requires.
@ref s 33(1) (src:440-465)
GIVEN unit IS A VicUnitCitedByNumberInASubordinateInstrument, instrumentContainsChapters IS A BOOLEAN, scheduleIsTheOnlyOne IS A BOOLEAN, contextOtherwiseRequires IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s33(1) a reference to a unit by number is construed as a reference to` MEANS
    IF contextOtherwiseRequires THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER unit
         WHEN VicSiChapter THEN JUST "the Chapter, designated by that number, of the subordinate instrument in which the reference occurs"
         WHEN VicSiPart THEN
             IF instrumentContainsChapters
             THEN JUST "the Part, designated by that number, of the Chapter in which the reference occurs"
             ELSE JUST "the Part, designated by that number, of the subordinate instrument in which the reference occurs"
         WHEN VicSiRegulationRuleByLawLocalLawOrSchedule THEN JUST "the regulation, rule, by-law, local law or Schedule, designated by that number, of or to the subordinate instrument in which the reference occurs"
         WHEN VicSiScheduleNotCitedByNumber THEN
             IF scheduleIsTheOnlyOne
             THEN JUST "the Schedule to the subordinate instrument in which the reference occurs"
             ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN VicSiDivision THEN JUST "the Division, designated by that number, of the Part in which the reference occurs"
         WHEN VicSiSubdivision THEN JUST "the Subdivision, designated by that number, of the Division in which the reference occurs"
         WHEN VicSiSubregulationOrClauseOfARegulation THEN JUST "the subregulation or clause, designated by that number, of the regulation in which the reference occurs"
         WHEN VicSiSubruleOrClauseOfARule THEN JUST "the subrule or clause, designated by that number, of the rule in which the reference occurs"
         WHEN VicSiClauseOfAByLawOrLocalLaw THEN JUST "the clause, designated by that number, of the by-law or local law in which the reference occurs"
         WHEN VicSiParagraphOfAProvisionInterpretationOrSchedule THEN JUST "the paragraph, designated by that number, of the regulation, rule, by-law, local law, subregulation, subrule, clause of a by-law, local law, clause, subclause, interpretation or Schedule in which the reference occurs"
         WHEN VicSiParagraphOfAClauseSubclauseItemColumnTableOrFormInASchedule THEN JUST "the paragraph, designated by that number, of the clause, subclause, item, column, table or form or in the Schedule in which the reference occurs"
         WHEN VicSiSubparagraph THEN JUST "the subparagraph, designated by that number, of the paragraph in which the reference occurs"
         WHEN VicSiSubSubparagraph THEN JUST "the sub-subparagraph, designated by that number, of the subparagraph in which the reference occurs"
         WHEN VicSiClauseItemColumnTableOrFormOfASchedule THEN JUST "the clause, item, column, table or form, designated by that number, of or in the Schedule in which the reference occurs"
         WHEN VicSiSubclause THEN JUST "the subclause, designated by that number, of the clause in which the reference occurs"
         WHEN VicSiSubSubclause THEN JUST "the sub-subclause, designated by that number, of the subclause in which the reference occurs"

DECLARE VicHowAUnitIsDesignatedInASubordinateInstrument IS ONE OF
    VicSiANumberExpressedInWordsOrFigures
    VicSiALetter
    VicSiACombinationOfANumberSoExpressedAndALetter
    VicSiSomethingElseAsADesignation

-- s 33(2): in subsection (1) number means a number expressed in words or figures, a letter, or a combination of such a number and a letter.
-- src:466 | (2) In subsection (1) number means—
-- src:467 | (a) a number expressed in words or figures;
-- src:468 | (b) a letter;
-- src:469 | (c) a combination of a number so expressed and a letter.
@ref s 33(2) (src:466-469)
GIVEN designation IS A VicHowAUnitIsDesignatedInASubordinateInstrument
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s33(2) the designation is a number for s 33(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER designation
    WHEN VicSiSomethingElseAsADesignation THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 34 Construction of references in subordinate instruments to portions of subordinate instruments or Acts`

-- s 34: a description or citation of a portion of a subordinate instrument, another instrument or an Act is, unless the contrary intention appears, construed as including the word, regulation, rule, ... mentioned as forming the beginning and as forming the end of the portion.
-- src:472 | 34 Construction of references in subordinate instruments to portions of subordinate instruments or Acts
-- src:473 | In a subordinate instrument, a description or citation of a portion of that subordinate instrument or of any other subordinate instrument or of any Act shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as including the word, regulation, rule, by-law, subregulation, subrule, clause, section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, Chapter, Part, Schedule or other Division mentioned or referred to as forming the beginning and as forming the end of the portion comprised in the description or citation.
@ref s 34 (src:472-473)
GIVEN firstPosition IS A NUMBER, lastPosition IS A NUMBER, position IS A NUMBER, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s34 the division at a position is within the portion cited` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        IF position AT LEAST firstPosition AND position AT MOST lastPosition THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
